'''Torre CBNM''' is a 46-storey office tower in [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. At approximately 200 metres (656 ft) tall, it is the second-tallest building in [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], the third-tallest in [[Sant Cristòfor]], and the third-tallest in [[Balboa]]. It is a prominent landmark on the waterfront skyline. The building is owned by [[Corporació Bancària del Nou Món]] (CBNM), which uses the tower as one of its principal headquarters facilities.

The tower is distinguished by its asymmetrical massing, a rectangular glass podium, and a slender tower shaft that rises from one side of the base rather than from the centre. Its reflective blue curtain wall glazing and sail-like crown give the building a strong visual identity in the Sant Cristòfor skyline.

== Architecture ==

Torre CBNM consists of two primary masses. The lower podium is a rectangular glass base of roughly 10 to 12 storeys, clad in blue-green curtain wall glazing. It establishes a broad street presence and contains the tower's lobby, retail space, parking, and lower office floors. Rising from one side of the podium is a slender office shaft with darker reflective glazing than the base. The shaft's vertical proportions emphasise height rather than bulk, while mechanical floors are integrated into the facade rather than expressed externally.

The tower's upper profile is defined by a sharply sloping roof that forms a sail-like crown. This feature, together with the asymmetric placement of the tower shaft, gives the building a distinctive silhouette on the waterfront.

== Use ==

Torre CBNM serves as an office building for [[Corporació Bancària del Nou Món]]. The tower houses executive offices, corporate departments, and client-facing services associated with the bank's operations in Sant Cristòfor.

